items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:17:  thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal: mathematical-premise
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:36:Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H,K$ be complex Hilbert spaces, let $(M_a)_{a\ge1}$ be bounded operators on $K$ with $\sum_{a\le N}M_a^*M_a\to I_K$ strongly, and let $R$ be a trace-class operator on $H\widehat\otimes K$. In this statement, $R\ge0$ means that $R$ is self-adjoint and $\langle Rx,x\rangle\ge0$ for every $x$, as in [[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]]. Then the series (when either factor is $\{0\}$, use the zero partial-trace maps $\operatorname{Tr}_K:\mathcal S_1(\{0\})\to\mathcal S_1(H)$ and $\operatorname{Tr}_H:\mathcal S_1(\{0\})\to\mathcal S_1(K)$; when both factors are nonzero, use the partial traces of [[lem-nrqm-composites-separable-partial-trace]])
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:40:converges in trace norm, its sum $\Phi(R)$ is trace class with $\operatorname{tr}\Phi(R)=\operatorname{tr}R$ and $\Phi(R)\ge0$ if $R\ge0$, and the reduced state on $H$ is unchanged:
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:48:**Given:** $H,K$; the family $(M_a)$; a trace-class $R$ on $H\widehat\otimes K$ with nuclear representation $R=\sum_jT_{w_j,z_j}$; a bounded $A\in\mathcal B(H)$.
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:52:[F2] Under the strong completeness hypothesis, $\sum_aV_aRV_a^*$ converges in trace norm for every trace-class $R$, is positive for positive $R$, and preserves the trace, where $V_a:=I_H\otimes M_a$; moreover the identity $\operatorname{tr}\bigl(\sum_aV_aRV_a^*\bigr)=\operatorname{tr}R$ is the trace-preservation clause ([[lem-nrqm-composites-countable-kraus-normalization]], [[lem-nrqm-composites-finite-ancilla-complete-positivity]]).
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:56:[F4] For a bounded operator $B$ and trace-class $T$, $BT$ is trace class with $\|BT\|_1\le\|B\|\,\|T\|_1$, and $\operatorname{tr}(BT)$ is linear in $T$ and continuous in trace norm ([[thm-trace-class-is-a-two-sided-banach-operator-ideal]], [[thm-trace-is-absolutely-convergent-and-basis-independent]]). In addition, every trace-class $T$ has a nuclear representation $T=\sum_jT_{w_j,z_j}$, and for bounded $B$ the trace formulas $\operatorname{tr}(TB)=\sum_j\langle w_j,B^*z_j\rangle=\operatorname{tr}(BT)$ hold with absolute convergence ([[lem-nrqm-composites-nuclear-bounded-cyclicity]], Facts [F2] and Statement (b)).
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:60:1.1 [Convergence of the local map] If $H=\{0\}$ or $K=\{0\}$, then $R=0$ and every summand $(I_H\otimes M_a)R(I_H\otimes M_a)^*$ is zero; hence $\Phi(R)=0$ and both sides of $\operatorname{Tr}_K\Phi(R)=\operatorname{Tr}_KR$ are zero by the convention in the Statement. Assume henceforth $H,K\ne\{0\}$. By [F1] the amplified family satisfies the strong completeness hypothesis of [F2] on the Hilbert space $H\widehat\otimes K$, so the series $\sum_aV_aRV_a^*$ with $V_a=I_H\otimes M_a$ converges in trace norm, its sum $\Phi(R)$ is trace class with $\operatorname{tr}\Phi(R)=\operatorname{tr}R$, and $\Phi(R)\ge0$ for $R\ge0$. [given, F1, F2]
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:62:2.1 [Pairing computation] For bounded $A$ and $V_a=I_H\otimes M_a$, apply the bounded cyclicity of [F4] to the trace-class operator $T=RV_a^*(A\otimes I_K)$ and bounded $V_a$. It gives $\operatorname{tr}\bigl(V_aRV_a^*(A\otimes I_K)\bigr)=\operatorname{tr}\bigl(R\,V_a^*(A\otimes I_K)V_a\bigr)$ with $V_a^*(A\otimes I_K)V_a=(I_H\otimes M_a^*)(A\otimes I_K)(I_H\otimes M_a)=A\otimes M_a^*M_a$. For each $N$, sum this identity over $a\le N$; trace-norm convergence of the series in step 1.1 and trace-norm continuity of the bounded trace pairing [F4] give $\operatorname{tr}(\Phi(R)(A\otimes I_K))=\lim_{N\to\infty}\operatorname{tr}(R(A\otimes S_N))$, where $S_N=\sum_{a\le N}M_a^*M_a$. [step 1.1, F4, algebra]
items/lem-nrqm-composites-local-trace-preserving-no-signalling.md:66:4.1 [Conclusion] By [F3], $\operatorname{tr}\bigl((\operatorname{Tr}_K\Phi(R))A\bigr)=\operatorname{tr}(\Phi(R)(A\otimes I_K))=\operatorname{tr}(R(A\otimes I_K))=\operatorname{tr}((\operatorname{Tr}_KR)A)$ for every bounded $A$; since the pairings with all $A$ determine a trace-class operator by the uniqueness in [F3], $\operatorname{Tr}_K\Phi(R)=\operatorname{Tr}_KR$. The statement for the first factor is obtained by exchanging the roles of $H$ and $K$. [step 3.1, F3] ∎
