Let $\Gamma$ act by $+1$ on every $+$ block and by $-1$ on every $-$ block. Then $D(Q)$ is dense, $Q$ is self-adjoint and odd in the sense $Q\Gamma=-\Gamma Q$ on $D(Q)$. Its square $H:=Q^2$ is a nonnegative self-adjoint diagonal operator equal to $0$ on $\mathcal H_0^+\oplus\mathcal H_0^-$ and to $\lambda I$ on each positive block, with domain $\{\psi:\sum_{\lambda\in\Sigma}\lambda^2\|\psi_\lambda\|^2<\infty\}$.

## Statement references

[Martin, §§1 and 7.1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/9709356v7).

[Gates et al., §§3.2–3.3 and 8.4](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0108200).

Hilbert space: [[def-hilbert-space]].

Real and complex inner-product spaces and their induced length: [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]].

Unbounded linear operators: domain, graph and extension: [[def-unbounded-linear-operator-domain-and-graph]].

Adjoint of a densely defined operator: [[def-adjoint-of-a-densely-defined-unbounded-operator]].

Symmetric, self-adjoint and essentially self-adjoint operators: [[def-symmetric-self-adjoint-and-essentially-self-adjoint]].

Square roots exist: a unique $\sqrt{a} \ge 0$ with $(\sqrt{a})^2 = a$; the positives are $\{x^2 : x \neq 0\}$: [[thm-of-square-roots]].

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The orthogonal decomposition, finite-support density, finite-dimensional blocks and block unitaries stated above. Assume Countable Choice as required by the imported unbounded-adjoint and self-adjoint definitions.

## Statement

Let $\mathcal H$ carry an irreducible positive unitary super-Poincare representation with metric $\eta=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, future-cone support and the charge-domain reduction conditions stated in its definition. Let $\mathcal C_+^*$ be the closed future cone from the representation definition and define $s:\mathcal C_+^*\to[0,\infty)$ by $s(p)=-\eta^{\mu\nu}p_\mu p_\nu$. For Borel $A\subseteq[0,\infty)$ define $F(A)=E(\{p\in\mathcal C_+^*:s(p)\in A\})$. Then every supercharge and its adjoint reduce each mass-squared spectral subspace: if $\psi\in D(Q)\cap\operatorname{ran}F(A)$ then $Q\psi\in\operatorname{ran}F(A)$, and the same holds for $Q^*$. Moreover there is a unique $m^2\ge0$ such that $F(A)=I$ when $m^2\in A$ and $F(A)=0$ when $m^2\notin A$. Thus the nonnegative mass $m=\sqrt{m^2}$ is constant throughout the irreducible multiplet. For a nonzero supercharge image, the source and image lie in the same mass spectral sector. No sharp-momentum eigenvector or rest frame is assumed in the full Hilbert space. If an additional group acts unitarily and commutes with the supercharges on their invariant domains, each supercharge also intertwines that group action; no gauge-charge conclusion is asserted without this extra hypothesis.

## Statement references

[Martin, §1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ph/9709356v7).

[Gates et al., §3.3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0108200).

Positive unitary super-Poincare representation with spectral-domain covariance: [[def-qftx-unitary-super-poincare-representation]].

Projection valued measure: [[def-projection-valued-measure]].

[F2] [[def-projection-valued-measure]]: each $E(B)$ is an orthogonal projection and $E$ is strongly countably additive on disjoint Borel sets.

[F3] [[lem-scalar-and-complex-measures-from-a-pvm]]: for any unit vector $\psi$, $\mu_\psi(A)=\langle F(A)\psi,\psi\rangle$ is a countably additive probability measure once $F$ is a normalized PVM.

[F4] [[thm-of-square-roots]]: every nonnegative real number has a unique nonnegative square root.

[A1] Assume Countable Choice, as required by the PVM and scalar-measure suppliers used here ([[def-countable-choice]]).

## Proof

**Proof technique:** direct.

