items/ex-qftx-n2-shortened-rest-fiber.md:81:2.1 For the same-flavor pairs, two annihilators or two creators anticommute by step 1.1, so their central bracket is zero. The two nonzero distinct-flavor brackets are $\{Q^1_1,Q^2_2\}=2M e^{i\phi}\{a_1,a_1^*\}=2zI$ and $\{Q^1_2,Q^2_1\}=-2M e^{i\phi}\{a_2,a_2^*\}=-2zI$. Every other distinct-flavor pair is either a distinct-mode anticommutator or a square of one creation/annihilation operator, and so has zero anticommutator. These are exactly $2\epsilon_{\alpha\beta}Z^{IJ}$ with $\epsilon_{12}=1$ and antisymmetric $Z$; taking Hilbert adjoints gives the conjugate barred relations. [F1, step 1.1, algebra]
items/ex-qftx-n1-supercharge-oscillator.md:40:Let $M>0$ and let $\mathcal H=\Lambda^*\mathbb C^2$ have orthonormal occupation basis $|n_1,n_2\rangle$ for $n_1,n_2\in\{0,1\}$. Define fermionic annihilation operators by $a_1|n_1,n_2\rangle=n_1|0,n_2\rangle$ and $a_2|n_1,n_2\rangle=(-1)^{n_1}n_2|n_1,0\rangle$, and let $a_\alpha^*$ be their Hilbert adjoints. Set $P^0=MI$, $P^j=0$, all central charges to zero, and $Q_\alpha=\sqrt{2M}a_\alpha$, $\bar Q_{\dot\alpha}=Q_\alpha^*$ with dotted index corresponding to the same $\alpha$. Give $\mathcal H$ the parity $(-1)^{n_1+n_2}$. This finite-dimensional rest fiber is a positive representation of the N=1 supercharge anticommutators in the stated mostly-plus convention; it has two even and two odd states. Use natural units $\hbar=c=1$, so $M$ has mass dimension one and each displayed supercharge has mass dimension one-half. It is only a rest-algebra fiber and asserts no full spacetime representation.
items/def-qftx-n1-chiral-superfield.md:55:For external odd constant parameters $\epsilon^\alpha,\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}$ that anticommute with the odd generators and coefficient algebra, set $\delta_{\epsilon,\bar\epsilon}\Phi=\sum_\alpha\epsilon^\alpha Q_\alpha\Phi+\sum_{\dot\alpha}\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}\bar Q_{\dot\alpha}\Phi$. The component transformation is, by definition, the unique ordered-basis coefficient tuple of this transformed superfield in the displayed $y,\theta$ expansion. The space of fields is classical and smooth, so these differential operations have common domain $\mathscr S$; no quantum-field operator domain or field equation is assumed. In natural units $[x^\mu]=-1$ and $[\theta]=[\bar\theta]=-\tfrac12$. If $[\Phi]=d$ is assigned, the formal component dimensions are $[A]=d$, $[\psi_\alpha]=d+\tfrac12$, and $[F]=d+1$; no value of $d$ is fixed. In the same natural-unit convention, $D_\alpha$, $\bar D_{\dot\alpha}$, $Q_\alpha$ and $\bar Q_{\dot\alpha}$ have mass dimension $+\tfrac12$, while $[\epsilon^\alpha]=[\bar\epsilon^{\dot\alpha}]=-\tfrac12$, so $\delta_{\epsilon,\bar\epsilon}$ is dimensionless.
items/thm-qftx-supermultiplet-mass-degeneracy.md:42:Let $\mathcal H$ carry an irreducible positive unitary super-Poincare representation with metric $\eta=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, future-cone support and the charge-domain reduction conditions stated in its definition. Let $\mathcal C_+^*$ be the closed future cone from the representation definition and define $s:\mathcal C_+^*\to[0,\infty)$ by $s(p)=-\eta^{\mu\nu}p_\mu p_\nu$. For Borel $A\subseteq[0,\infty)$ define $F(A)=E(\{p\in\mathcal C_+^*:s(p)\in A\})$. Then every supercharge and its adjoint reduce each mass-squared spectral subspace: if $\psi\in D(Q)\cap\operatorname{ran}F(A)$ then $Q\psi\in\operatorname{ran}F(A)$, and the same holds for $Q^*$. Moreover there is a unique $m^2\ge0$ such that $F(A)=I$ when $m^2\in A$ and $F(A)=0$ when $m^2\notin A$. Thus the nonnegative mass $m=\sqrt{m^2}$ is constant throughout the irreducible multiplet. Use natural units $\hbar=c=1$, so $m$ has mass dimension one and $m^2$ has mass dimension two. For a nonzero supercharge image, the source and image lie in the same mass spectral sector. No sharp-momentum eigenvector or rest frame is assumed in the full Hilbert space. If an additional group acts unitarily and commutes with the supercharges on their invariant domains, each supercharge also intertwines that group action; no gauge-charge conclusion is asserted without this extra hypothesis.

